{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-processes-year-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.68, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-processes-year`: `scale-county-timeagg-processes-month`'s selections -- every on-road process a county inventory selects, the evaporative ones and refueling among them -- at the same four months, day types and hours, with `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Year\"/>`, over the same county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`). MOVESOutput is 19,628 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is PreAggYEAR.sql (`scale-county-timeagg-year`, PLAN.md §7.3.65) for the evaporative and refueling processes: TankFuelGenerator's gasohol share and RefuelingLossCalculator's average RVP and energy content are SUMS over FuelSupply's summed shares, the vapor venting and refueling temperatures the MonthWeighting mean, and the evaporative SourceHours, SHO and soak shares over the whole-year cell. PreAggYEAR.sql's AverageTankTemperature and SoakActivityFraction sections find both tables empty, as PreAggDAY.sql's and PreAggMONTH.sql's do: no generator has written them yet, so permeation again has no row (PLAN.md §7.3.64).\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1 and `db_aggregationmonth` the RunSpec's months (`tools/runspec-month-selection.py`), as in `scale-county-timeagg-year`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 19628, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs of the one (county, month, day) cell, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step",
      "evaporative",
      "refueling",
      "crankcase",
      "brake-wear",
      "tire-wear",
      "year-aggregation"
    ]
  },
